course: dictionary
lesson: 9684
title: Suffer: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To suffer means to feel pain, illness, sadness or other bad things. «People suffered in wars and famines» means they went through very hard times, because wars and famines are bad things. The clues around the word tell you its meaning.
explain: Suffer can also mean to have a bad thing happen to you, as in «suffer a defeat» or «suffer damage». A team that loses a match has suffered a defeat, and a car hit by a stone may suffer damage.
explain: Suffer can mean to get worse because of something. «Your work will suffer if you do not sleep» means your work will become poorer if you are tired. To check, swap in your meaning: "your work will get worse if you do not sleep" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Suffer means to feel pain, illness, sadness or other bad things.
fact: «Suffer from» is a useful phrase: people suffer from hay fever or asthma.
fact: «Suffer in silence» means to bear pain or sadness quietly, without complaining.
fact: «The Black Death of the 14th century» spread along trade routes to Europe, and «China also suffered epidemics in that century».
fact: When a factory closes, «local shops suffer too», because the workers have less money to spend.
exercise: «People suffered in wars and famines.» What does suffered mean here? | Ate a lot of food | Won easily | Moved to a new house | *Went through pain and hardship
exercise: «Your work will suffer if you do not sleep.» What does suffer mean in this sentence? | *Get worse | Go faster | Sleep more | Get better
exercise: «Animals suffer if they are not cared for.» Find and copy the verb in this sentence. | animals | for | cared | *suffer
test: «When the factory closed, local shops suffered too.» What does suffered mean? | *Were harmed and lost customers and money | Opened more shops | Were given free gifts | Grew bigger
test: Which word completes this? People suffer ___ hay fever. | across | into | onto | *from
exam: Mei says «suffer in silence» means to shout loudly about pain. What does the phrase really mean? | To be happy at night | *To bear pain quietly, without complaining | To shout loudly about pain | To suffer in a silent cinema
